# Scripted server wire: the provider CLI in its documented JSON-RPC 2.0 server
# mode, newline-delimited over stdio (adaptadores-propios-acp design D6,
# re-anchored to codex-cli 0.156.1 by codex-al-dia).
#
# Every method, notification and field below is taken from the schema the
# official CLI dumps for itself, vendored verbatim in
# `../schemas/codex-app-server/` (see its PROVENANCE.md), and the ORDER of the
# lines follows the transcript of the real 0.156.1 server recorded on
# 2026-09-24 and vendored beside this file
# (`codex-app-server-0.156.1.transcript.ndjson`). The conformance test of the
# adapter validates each line against the dump and checks that the script's
# sequence of methods is an ordered subsequence of the transcript's, so this
# fixture cannot drift away from the contract, or from the real order, in
# silence.
#
# Where this script differs from the recording, on purpose and only here:
#
#   * The approval is granted and the file change completes; in the recording
#     it was declined.
#   * The thread comes back under the gate the adapter asks for (`untrusted`,
#     `user`, a read-only sandbox without network), which is what the real
#     server answered when asked (measured 2026-09-24); the vendored recording
#     was taken without asking, and shows the maintainer's own `on-request`.
#   * Ids, paths, texts and the model are the ones the end-to-end tests pin.
#   * Fields the real server sends that the stable dump does not declare
#     (`runtimeWorkspaceRoots`, `activePermissionProfile`, `multiAgentMode`,
#     and in the thread `environments`, `extra`, `canAcceptDirectInput`,
#     `daybreakEnabled`) are left out: the adapter relies on nothing the dump
#     does not declare.
#
# What the recording settled that the 0.77.0 fixture had to guess:
#
#   * The `turn/start` answer arrives FIRST, still `inProgress`, and the turn
#     ends on `turn/completed`. The adapter ends its turn on whichever terminal
#     signal arrives first; the adverse ordering (answer last) stays covered by
#     its unit tests.
#   * The server echoes the user's own message back as a `userMessage` item.
#     The prompt is already on the record, so the adapter shows nothing for it.
#   * Status, token usage and resolved-request notifications interleave with
#     the turn. The adapter maps none of them; they are here to prove that
#     ignoring them costs nothing.
#   * MCP servers from the CLI's own configuration report their startup around
#     the turn's answer. The adapter names each one in the session, once.
#   * Every connection reports the CLI's remote control before the thread's
#     answer. Off, as here, it costs nothing; anything else refuses the session.
#   * The server announces the session's own thread once the first turn is
#     asked for. It is the session's, so the adapter says nothing about it; a
#     thread whose parent is the session's would get a row.
#   * Responses carry no `"jsonrpc"` member and notifications carry an
#     `emittedAtMs` member beside `params`. This fixture sends `"jsonrpc"`
#     because JSON-RPC 2.0 requires it and omits `emittedAtMs`; the adapter
#     tolerates both forms.
#   * The scripted wire numbers its own requests from 1, so the resolved
#     request is 1 where the recording said 0.
#
# 1. Handshake: the user agent is still the only version the wire offers. The
#    CLI now puts the client's own name where `codex_cli_rs` used to be.
{"mock":"await-request","method":"initialize"}
{"mock":"respond","result":{"userAgent":"meltemi-codex-acp/0.156.1 (mock-codex-wire; scripted) unknown (meltemi-codex-acp; 0.1.1)","codexHome":"/mock/codex-home","platformFamily":"unix","platformOs":"linux"}}
# 2. A thread is the conversation the ACP session maps onto.
{"mock":"await-request","method":"thread/start"}
{"mock":"notify","method":"remoteControl/status/changed","params":{"status":"disabled","serverName":"mock-machine","installationId":"mock-installation","environmentId":null}}
{"mock":"respond","result":{"thread":{"id":"mock-thread-1","sessionId":"mock-thread-1","forkedFromId":null,"parentThreadId":null,"preview":"","ephemeral":false,"section":null,"sectionEnteredAt":null,"projectId":null,"historyMode":"paginated","modelProvider":"mock","model":"mock-model","reasoningEffort":"xhigh","createdAt":1790000000,"updatedAt":1790000000,"recencyAt":1790000000,"status":{"type":"idle"},"path":"/mock/codex-home/sessions/mock-thread-1.jsonl","cwd":"/mock/project","cliVersion":"0.156.1","originator":"meltemi-codex-acp","source":"vscode","threadSource":null,"agentNickname":null,"agentRole":null,"gitInfo":null,"name":null,"turns":[]},"model":"mock-model","modelProvider":"mock","serviceTier":"default","disabledPluginIds":[],"cwd":"/mock/project","instructionSources":[],"approvalPolicy":"untrusted","approvalsReviewer":"user","sandbox":{"type":"readOnly","networkAccess":false},"reasoningEffort":"xhigh"}}
